title mycelium Till — a contested draw decided by the agreed order (r1)
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the 1024-round road and the six-season double-seat; approve own design rounds; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates.
think The Mycelium Tenure arc closed (r1 verdict · r2 travels · r3 across a Knot · r4 true), and both tenure.rye and tenure_knot.rye name the same next crux in their own headers: a double-spend loser as a lawful no-op. That is the Lindy-first crux-first move — it completes the consensus ledger's verdict logic and is exactly Season D's promise (improving on TigerBeetle and Mysticeti), fully agent-doable (composes cord + fold public API, demo seeds, no gate).
think Grounded the design in the real fund model by reading fold.rye: the treasury is a GLOBAL supply (issued − taxed), not per-account balances. So the truest double-spend this ledger carries is a supply-exhaustion race — two spends each affordable alone against the treasury, not both. The honest distinction that separates a lost race from never-could-pay is monotonic and position-respecting: issued-so-far (issues only add, no release), the high-water mark of everything the treasury could ever have paid by a fact's turn.
think fold.fold_fact returns one Overdraw for both cases and does NOT mutate state on the reserve/tax overdraw path, so at the catch site state.issued is exactly issued-so-far. amount <= issued-so-far → the coins existed once, an earlier draw took them → lawful no-op spent-out loss, folding continues. amount > issued-so-far → a demand no order could meet → refuse whole. An issue overdraw is a u64 wrap, never a race → poison unconditionally.
think Named the module the Till (comlink-tendency: clear, fun, safe; grepped mycelium/ mantra/ pond/ tally/ comlink/ — zero collision) — the drawer a treasury's coins sit in; two hands reach in, the first takes what is there, the second finds it emptied and breaks nothing. A warm mirror of the Tenure (one name, one holder → one till, one draw).
obs r1 self-approved design round (active-designing/20260813-064129_…) then mycelium/till.rye grown beside cord/fold/tenure, editing none. resolve walks the committed order one fact at a time through fold.fold_fact; an accepted tax/reserve records a winning Draw; an Overdraw with amount <= issued_here records a ShortDraw; a greedy overdraw / broken signature / StarTaken each refuse whole. A StarTaken refuses here on purpose — a name-contest is the Tenure's verdict, and the Till reads coins, not names; a mixed log is resolved twice, each module honest to its own resource.
obs Selftest crux: a treasury of 1000, an uncontested tax of 100, two keepers each taxing 700 — across three arrival permutations the same later-sorting keeper comes up short (draws=2, short=1, supply folds once to 200, total_lost 700), and the loss is proven lawful (amount <= issued_at). A 5000 tax against 1000 issued refuses Overdraw (never-could-pay); a tampered signature refuses IdentityRefused. GREEN first pass.
obs Reconciled the design doc with the code in the same round (docs-implementation-sync): during implementation I chose the Till refuses StarTaken whole rather than composing Tenure, so fixed the doc's StarTaken decision section and the boundaries line (composes cord + fold; the Tenure is design kin, not a code dep). Witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0.
file active-designing/20260813-064129_mycelium-till-double-spend-exploration.md self-approved design capture — the Till, the crux, the four rounds
file mycelium/till.rye r1 — resolve a committed Dag into a Till: winning draws, spent-out losses (lawful no-op), never-could-pay + corruption refuse whole
file tools/mycelium_till_witness.rish r1 witness — verdict · arrival-order independence · lawful no-op · never-could-pay/corruption poison; Cord + fold stand at the door
recommend keep-going the Till r1 crux stands (contested draw decided by the agreed order); next the Till arc r2 (the verdict travels as a format till-v1 Bron record) mirroring tenure_bron, then r3 across a Knot, r4 a real double-spend fixture true. Per-account balances and a served Till stay named horizons behind the gates.
